    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d453">

                <pb facs="0494" n="460" sameAs="frus:frus1897/pg460"/>

                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Sir Julian Pauncefote
                        to Mr. Sherman.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1897-04-05"><hi rendition="#italic">April 5,
                        1897</hi></date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I have the honor to acknowledge the receipt
                    of your note No. 630, of the 3d instant, respecting the proposed ordinance for
                    the disposal of men-of-war’s men who offend against the municipal regulations in
                    Samoa and the course which you propose to follow with reference thereto.</p>
                <p>I have forwarded a copy of your note to the Marquis of Salisbury.</p>
                <p>I have, etc.,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Julian
                    Pauncefote.</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
